A||||8||filthyscarecrow||more turbo questions||||1||
Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||11-17-2001||08:03 PM||||1. okay, the first question i'm sure has been asked before. doyou guys run EGR with the turbo? mine will be intercooled, so intake charge temp shouldn't be an issue, but i know EGR cools the combustion chamber temp. (i've been workin on a new intake too, and plumbing EGR might be an additional hassle). <BR>2. anyone usign an AFC form either A'pexi or HKS? what size injectors are you using? i'm having a helluva time finding 310-330cc injectors (the size i will probably need). would it work to run 450cc injectors from, say, a DSM and then use the AFC to reduce the fuel going in to the proper amount, rather than the traditional way of using the AFC to increase fuel flow? i can get 8 DSM injectors for $70 and use ballast resistors so they'll work with the fiero ECM. i think they're the same body type as fiero injectors. if anyone knows for sure, let me know. <BR>3. i know many people use the MSD 6BTM for turbo setups, but crane has one that has boost proportional retard too, and i like the crane ignition better, but i don't know how well it will work. the details of the boost retard are sketchy at best. anyone used this setup? i believe it requires a 2 bar map sensor, but we've got a bunch of those lying around the the race shop. GM gives us all kinds of sensors every year for sponsorship... <BR>4. fuel pumps? will an in-line pump work? we've got spares of those as well. <BR>5. EPROMS. who can burn EPROMS? is this easier than all the extra ignition/fuel computer crap, or is it the same hassle? i imagine the AFC would be easier because i wouldn't have to rewrite EPROMS after tuning it, ad infinitum. <P>alright, i've picked enough brains for one day, time to go pick some noses... thanks guys.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-17-2001||10:22 PM||||Have you thought about useing a HKS "SIC"-"SFIC" Secondary Injector Controler - Secondary Fuel Injector Controler or something long those lines? Is't cost is about $1000-1500 and it is a stand alone "black box" that can run a second set of injectors. It could be turned on by a boost controler so that your 2nd set of injectors only comes on at a set point say 10psi. This would alow you to run a "Normal" amount of boost for the street and then step it up at the track and keep it streetable at low boost.<P>I don't have any help on the EGR. <P>as for the AFC I have seen the Apexi S-AFC in other GM cars that use the same type MAP sensor as us, But I don't know how well it works as I have never seen one working & inuse. But I would like to know if it can work.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOYPICS/scrapbookFiles/importD3.gif"> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A> <A HREF="mailto:Tomtom81@webtv.net">Tomtom81@webtv.net</A> ||||reg||1
